# After a WAL shard restart its in-memory entries are gone. Accepting an append
# from a leaf whose entry is not loaded, instead of rejecting it until the leaf
# re-presents its claim, accepts a stale epoch.
MODULE: StaleEpochNeverAppendsUnloadedEntryAccepted
TARGET: StaleEpochNeverAppends
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the restarted shard accepts an append whose entry it has not reloaded
PERTURBS: OwnAlloc
BOUNDS: WithRestart = TRUE

--- FIND
    /\ memFence > 0
    /\ epoch[a] >= memFence
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: an unloaded entry does not hold the append.
    /\ epoch[a] >= memFence
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END